DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 0, 9, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 15, 4, 13 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 5, 5, 14 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<15, 4, 13>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<15, 4, 13>") x Compute("<0, 9, 0>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<0, 9, 0>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 5, 14>") . Compute("<15, 4, 13>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 4, 10, 19 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 16, 11, 20 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<16, 11, 20>") x Compute("<4, 10, 19>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<16, 11, 20>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<4, 10, 19>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<4, 10, 19>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 5, 6, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, 7, 6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, 7, 6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<5, 6, 0>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<5, 6, 0>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, 7, 6>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 2, 10, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 17, 17, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 15, 16, 2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<15, 16, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<15, 16, 2>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<15, 16, 2>") . Compute("<17, 17, 10>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<15, 16, 2>") x Compute("<17, 17, 10>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<15, 16, 2>") x Compute("<2, 10, 1>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<17, 17, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 12, 6, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 16, 7, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 12, 2, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<16, 7, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<16, 7, 1>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<12, 6, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<12, 2, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<12, 6, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
